"""Shared steps every generated feature file reuses.

The Framework Indexing Engine finds these first, so the code generator
never duplicates login / search / logout logic per transaction.

Every step here is registered with @step (matches ANY of Given/When/Then)
rather than @given/@when/@then. behave partitions its step registry BY
type and resolves "And"/"But" to whatever concrete keyword the PRECEDING
step in the same block used — e.g. feature.j2 renders the closing step as
"And user logs out" straight after "Then transaction ... completes
successfully", which resolves to a THEN step. A step registered with
@given only ever matches a Given-typed step, so that exact, correctly-
spelled step text still comes back "undefined" at run time. Since these
shared steps get reused across different feature files where the
preceding keyword (and therefore the resolved type) isn't fixed, @step is
the only decorator that's safe here.
"""
